breakpoint.yml:preflight	breakpoint.yml is in the frozen set hashed by .ci/breakpoint/MANIFEST.sha256 (workflow/breakpoint.yml) and must stay byte-identical in every repository that vendors breakpoint; check-breakpoint-drift.sh cmp's the live copy against the template, so a console-only profiler step would fail that gate. The session job is also runner-agnostic by design (runs-on is the dispatch input, chosen per session), so there is no single runner-label to arm the HOST_LEAK check with.
breakpoint.yml:session	breakpoint.yml is in the frozen set hashed by .ci/breakpoint/MANIFEST.sha256 (workflow/breakpoint.yml) and must stay byte-identical in every repository that vendors breakpoint; check-breakpoint-drift.sh cmp's the live copy against the template, so a console-only profiler step would fail that gate. The session job is also runner-agnostic by design (runs-on is the dispatch input, chosen per session), so there is no single runner-label to arm the HOST_LEAK check with.
